<section id="optimal-paths" class="process-section optimal-section">
  <div class="container process-shell-wide">
    <div class="process-heading">
      <span class="section-kicker">Optimal path computation</span>
      <h2>Optimal trust path computation.</h2>
      <p>
        Once admissible trust relationships are represented as a governed weighted
        graph, certification path selection becomes a shortest-path problem over valid
        candidates. PolarisChain optimizes path choice instead of accepting the first
        route returned by heuristic traversal.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-[minmax(0,0.96fr)_minmax(0,1.24fr)] gap-6 items-start max-[1180px]:grid-cols-[1fr]">
      <article class="bg-[rgba(18,24,37,0.62)] border border-[rgba(255,255,255,0.08)] rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] shadow-[0_18px_38px_rgba(0,0,0,0.18)] backdrop-blur-[12px] px-[26px] py-[28px] max-[760px]:p-[22px]">
        <span class="text-[rgba(196,188,175,0.72)] text-[0.76rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase">Objective function</span>
        <div class="mt-[18px] px-[18px] py-[20px] rounded-[18px] bg-[rgba(255,255,255,0.05)] border border-[rgba(255,255,255,0.08)] max-[760px]:mt-[16px] max-[760px]:px-[14px] max-[760px]:py-[16px]">
          <p class="block m-0 text-[#f5efe5] [font-family:'Cambria_Math','STIX_Two_Math','Times_New_Roman',serif] text-[clamp(1.34rem,1.9vw,1.72rem)] leading-[1.55] tracking-[0.01em] whitespace-normal break-words max-[760px]:text-[1.18rem] max-[760px]:leading-[1.5]" aria-label="P star equals arg min over P in Paths of the sum over e in P of w of e">
            <span class="italic">P</span>* = <span class="italic">argmin</span><sub class="text-[0.62em] align-[-0.42em]"><span class="italic">P</span> &isin; <span class="italic">Paths</span></sub>
            <span class="inline-block [transform:translateY(0.02em)]">&Sigma;</span><sub class="text-[0.62em] align-[-0.42em]"><span class="italic">e</span> &isin; <span class="italic">P</span></sub>
            <span class="italic">w</span>(<span class="italic">e</span>)
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-[18px] mb-0 mx-0 text-[rgba(215,206,193,0.78)] leading-[1.8]">
          Among all valid certification paths, the chosen route is the one with the
          minimum accumulated edge cost under the defined trust model.
        </p>
      </article>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-[repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))] gap-6 max-[1180px]:grid-cols-[1fr] max-[760px]:gap-[18px]">
        <article class="bg-[rgba(18,24,37,0.62)] border border-[rgba(255,255,255,0.08)] rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] shadow-[0_18px_38px_rgba(0,0,0,0.18)] backdrop-blur-[12px] p-6 min-h-full max-[760px]:p-[22px]">
          <h3 class="m-0 text-[#f3eee5] [font-family:'Playfair_Display',serif] text-[1.84rem] font-normal leading-[0.98] max-[760px]:text-[2.05rem]">Deterministic optimization</h3>
          <p class="mt-[18px] mb-0 mx-0 text-[rgba(215,206,193,0.78)] leading-[1.8]">
            Dijkstra-based computation is applied over the governed weighted graph so
            the selected trust path is the mathematically optimal route under the cost
            model, not a heuristic guess.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="bg-[rgba(18,24,37,0.62)] border border-[rgba(255,255,255,0.08)] rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] shadow-[0_18px_38px_rgba(0,0,0,0.18)] backdrop-blur-[12px] p-6 min-h-full max-[760px]:p-[22px]">
          <h3 class="m-0 text-[#f3eee5] [font-family:'Playfair_Display',serif] text-[1.84rem] font-normal leading-[0.98] max-[760px]:text-[2.05rem]">Multi-criteria scoring</h3>
          <p class="mt-[18px] mb-0 mx-0 text-[rgba(215,206,193,0.78)] leading-[1.8]">
            Edge weights can combine cryptographic profile, algorithm family, key
            strength, policy compatibility, and structural distance into a single
            comparable score.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="bg-[rgba(18,24,37,0.62)] border border-[rgba(255,255,255,0.08)] rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] shadow-[0_18px_38px_rgba(0,0,0,0.18)] backdrop-blur-[12px] p-6 min-h-full max-[760px]:p-[22px]">
          <h3 class="m-0 text-[#f3eee5] [font-family:'Playfair_Display',serif] text-[1.84rem] font-normal leading-[0.98] max-[760px]:text-[2.05rem]">Explainable trust paths</h3>
          <p class="mt-[18px] mb-0 mx-0 text-[rgba(215,206,193,0.78)] leading-[1.8]">
            Because each path is evaluated through explicit edge costs, the selected
            chain can be justified in terms of governance, cryptographic quality, and
            structural efficiency.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
